  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An organic compound gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>126</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> on complete combustion. If the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of carbon is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> then the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of hydrogen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> (Nearest integer)</p>"
  },
